00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  back here in the valley the original  federal eviction moratorium was set to  expire next thursday but the cdc decided  to extend it another month  this of course helps tenants who can't  afford rent but tonight we hear from a  landlord who lost out on thousands of  dollars but is doing her best to help  tenants  victoria saha has the story the cdc says  this is the last time the eviction  moratorium will be extended  meanwhile the nevada state eviction  moratorium ended earlier this month  and landlords are still making up for  the loss of income  although the extension of the eviction  moratorium comes as good news for  tenants  landlords like julie brown are left  scrambling to pick up the pieces  when they're not collecting those rents  they're not able to pay their mortgage  they're not able to pay their  insurance they're not able to pay their  taxes it was a hard year for many  landlords like herself who owns  properties across the valley  and rely on tenants rent as income but  brown says she wanted to work with her  tenants so they wouldn't be left on the  streets  every person has a story every house has  a story every home has a story  and we forget that these are real people  that have real challenges and  oftentimes they're humiliated she helped  reduce the rent or come up with a  payment plan  but brown says some tenants took  advantage of the eviction moratorium  and didn't pay rent at all even when  they had jobs  at one property she lost more than 30  thousand dollars  i do rely on that money to live and if  all of them had said can't pay  that would have been disastrous in all  during the eviction moratorium brown  says she lost  close to 70 thousand dollars last year  but she hasn't evicted anyone as of yet  if you are a resident facing eviction or  are behind on paying rent  legal experts say you shouldn't wait  until the federal eviction moratorium  ends  to get help victoria saha 8 news now  free legal help is available at the  civil self-help law center

